[49.329449, "o", "All the data is in hand. Here is the full qualification report.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Helm Preflight Upgrade Report\r\n\r\n### Verdict: 🔴 BLOCK — upgrade must not proceed\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Verdict** | `BLOCK` |\r\n| **Fingerprint** | `67c8f02774972c195947d2e4183295c9372bb96c8cbc92f042a689191d862010` |\r\n| **Tool** | helm-agent-preflight v0.1.0 (commit `91250d3`) |\r\n| **No deployment occurred** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n| **Rendering stability** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n| **Evidence completeness** | `COMPLETE` |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Diff Summary\r\n\r\n| Added | Modified | Removed |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| 0 | 1 | 0 |\r\n\r\n**Modified:** `ClusterRole/webapp-reader`\r\n- Path `$.rules` changed from explicit allow-list → full wildcard (`*`)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Security Findings (2 — both NEW, both CRITICAL)\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-001 — `ClusterRole/webapp-reader`\r\n- **JSON path:** `$.rules[0].resources`\r\n- **Message:** Wildcard `*` in resources grants access to **all** resource types\r\n- **Pre-existing:** `false` (introduced by this upgrade)\r\n- **Evaluator:** conftest\r\n\r\n#### [CRITICAL] RBAC-002 — `ClusterRole/webapp-reader`\r\n- **JSON path:** `$.rules[0].verbs`\r\n- **Message:** Wildcard `*` in verbs grants **all** operations\r\n- **Pre-existing:** `false` (introduced by this upgrade)\r\n- **Evaluator:** conftest\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Root Cause\r\n\r\nThe candidate chart (`examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml`) replaced the baseline's narrow permission set with a triple-wildcard rule:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# candidate (BLOCKED)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis grants the `webapp-reader` ClusterRole unrestricted access to every API group, resource type, and operation in the cluster — a critical RBAC escalation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Smallest Concrete Fix\r\n\r\nRevert the candidate's `rbac.yaml` rules to the baseline's explicit allow-list (or the minimal set the application actually needs):\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml\r\napiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1\r\nkind: ClusterRole\r\nmetadata:\r\n  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-reader\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What changed:** Replace `[\"*\"]` with the explicit values in `apiGroups`, `resources`, and `verbs`. No other file needs to change.\r\n\r\nIf the candidate chart legitimately needs additional permissions, add only the specific resources/verbs required — never use `*` wildcards in a ClusterRole.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> ⚠️ **Authorization required** before modifying any project files. Confirm and I will apply the fix and re-run preflight to verify a PASS verdict.\r\n"]
